/-!
# Properness of the projection of a projective bundle

Let `X` be a scheme and `ℰ` a finite locally free sheaf of modules on it. The projection

`π : 𝐏(ℰ) = Proj_X(Sym(ℰ)) ⟶ X`

of the projective bundle of `ℰ` is proper. This is the properness clause of Stacks 0800 for the
graded algebra `Sym(ℰ)`: its degree-zero part is the structure sheaf, hence a finite type
`𝒪_X`-module, and it is generated in degree one by `ℰ`, hence of finite type over its degree-zero
part.

The properness of the structure morphism of a relative `Proj` is already reduced to the affine
charts by `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.isProper_relativeProjToBase`, under two hypotheses on
every affine open `U` of the base: that the degree-zero part of the graded ring of sections over
`U` is `Γ(X, U)`, and that the ring of sections over `U` is a finite type algebra over that
degree-zero part. What this file supplies is both hypotheses for `Sym(ℰ)`.

## The two hypotheses, and what each costs

The degree-zero hypothesis is unconditional and is `Sym⁰(ℰ) = 𝒪_X`: the degree-zero
identification `SheafOfModules.sheafifiedSymmetricPieceZeroIso` carries the algebra unit to `1`,
which is what `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.bijective_smul_one_of_isoUnit` consumes. No
hypothesis on `ℰ` is used.

The finite type hypothesis splits in two. Generation in degree one is unconditional too, by
`Stacks.RelativeProj.adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top_symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent`;
what finiteness of `ℰ` is for is the remaining half, that the degree-one local sections over `U`
are spanned by finitely many of them. Degree one of `Sym(ℰ)` is `ℰ` itself, so this asks that
`Γ(ℰ, U)` be a finitely generated `Γ(X, U)`-module, which is false for an arbitrary
quasi-coherent `ℰ` and true for a finite locally free one — but only *locally* on the base, since
the local free presentations of `ℰ` are given on a cover that need not consist of affine opens.

So properness is proved on a cover rather than on every affine open:
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.isProper_relativeProjToBase_of_cover` asks for the two hypotheses
only at the members of a family of affine opens covering the base, which is enough because
properness is Zariski-local at the target. The cover used is the family of affine opens on which
`ℰ` is spanned by finitely many sections, and every point of `X` lies in such an affine open: it
lies in a member of the cover carrying a local free presentation, and the affine opens form a
basis.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.exists_finset_span_of_generatingSections`: the sections over
  an open `V` of a sheaf of modules which is free on finitely many generators over some open
  containing `V` are spanned by finitely many of them.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent_of_isFiniteLocallyFree`: a finite locally
  free sheaf of modules on a scheme is quasi-coherent.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data.isProper_toBase_of_cover` and
  `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.isProper_relativeProjToBase_of_cover`: **the structure morphism
  of a relative `Proj` is proper as soon as the chartwise hypotheses hold on a family of affine
  opens covering the base**, rather than on all of them.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.finiteType_sectionRing_of_adjoin_eq_top`: the section ring over
  `U` is a finite type algebra over its degree-zero part as soon as it is generated by its
  degree-one part and the degree-one local sections are spanned by finitely many of them. This is
  `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.finiteType_sectionRing` with the sheaf-level generation
  hypothesis replaced by its consequence on the section ring, which is the form available for a
  symmetric algebra.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.isIso_sectionRingZeroMap_symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent`: the
  degree-zero identification of every chart of a projective bundle is an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.isProper_projectiveBundleToBase`: **the projection of the projective
  bundle of a finite locally free sheaf of modules is proper.**

## Implementation notes

**Why the restricted-case attribute string.** Stacks 0800 asserts the equivalence of two
finiteness conditions on a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra `𝒜`, and that under them the
relative `Proj` of `𝒜` is locally projective and in particular proper. Only the properness
clause is proved here, and only for `𝒜 = Sym(ℰ)` with `ℰ` finite locally free. Local
projectivity, `AlgebraicGeometry.IsLocallyProjective`, would need a closed immersion of each
chart into a projective space over the base, hence the identification of the section ring of
`Sym(ℰ)` over an affine open `U` with `Sym_{Γ(X, U)}(ℰ(U))` — the affine case of Stacks 01CG.
The equivalence of the two finiteness conditions is a statement about a general graded algebra
whose degree-zero part is not the structure sheaf. The attribute therefore names the one case
proved.

**Scalars across a slice site.** A section of `ℰ.over W` over an object of `Over W` is a section
of `ℰ` over the underlying open, and the two scalar spellings `(R.over W).obj.obj (op V)` and
`R.obj.obj (op V.left)` are definitionally equal; they are not interchangeable for instance
synthesis, so the spanning statement is phrased existentially, with the type of the spanning
family fixed by the statement rather than inferred from the free presentation.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0800](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0800)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01OB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01C6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01C6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NQ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open TopologicalSpace DirectSum

universe v u w

/-! ### Degree zero of the symmetric algebra carries the unit to `1` -/

namespace PresheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {O : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w}}
  (F : PresheafOfModules.{w} (O ⋙ forget₂ _ RingCat))

/-- The degree-zero identification of the sectionwise symmetric algebra takes the algebra unit
to `1`. -/
theorem symmetricAlgebraPieceZeroIso_hom_one (W : Cᵒᵖ) :
    Hom.app (symmetricAlgebraPieceZeroIso F).hom W ((symPowIntOne F).eval W) =
      (1 : (O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w}).obj W) := by
  show SymmetricAlgebra.algebraMapInv
      (1 : SymmetricAlgebra ((O ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w}).obj W) (F.obj W)) = 1
  exact map_one _

end PresheafOfModules

namespace SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  {Osharp : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  (F : SheafOfModules.{w} (toRingCat J Osharp))

/-- **The degree-zero identification `Sym⁰(F) ≅ O` takes the algebra unit to `1`.** This is the
hypothesis of `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.bijective_smul_one_of_isoUnit` for a symmetric
algebra. -/
theorem sheafifiedSymmetricPieceZeroIso_one (W : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (sheafifiedSymmetricPieceZeroIso J F).hom.val.app W
        ((sheafifiedSymmetricAlgebra J F).one.eval W) =
      (1 : (toRingCat J Osharp).obj.obj W) := by
  refine (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyCounitIso_map_comp_apply (𝟙 (toRingCat J Osharp).obj)
    (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat J Osharp))
    (PresheafOfModules.symmetricAlgebraPieceZeroIso F.val).hom W
    ((PresheafOfModules.symPowIntOne F.val).eval W)).trans ?_
  exact PresheafOfModules.symmetricAlgebraPieceZeroIso_hom_one F.val W

end SheafOfModules

/-! ### Finitely many spanning sections -/

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- An isomorphism of sheaves of modules is sectionwise inverse on elements. -/
private theorem app_hom_app_inv_apply {C : Type*} [Category C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    {R : Sheaf J RingCat} {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules R} (e : M ≅ N) (W : Cᵒᵖ)
    (y : N.val.obj W) : e.hom.val.app W (e.inv.val.app W y) = y :=
  (by rw [e.inv_hom_id]; rfl : (e.inv ≫ e.hom).val.app W y = y)

/-- **A finite spanning family of local sections transports along an isomorphism of sheaves of
modules.** -/
theorem exists_finset_span_of_iso {M N : X.Modules} (e : M ≅ N) (V : X.Opens)
    (g : Finset (N.val.obj (op V)))
    (hg : Submodule.span (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) (g : Set (N.val.obj (op V))) = ⊤) :
    ∃ g' : Finset (M.val.obj (op V)),
      Submodule.span (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) (g' : Set (M.val.obj (op V))) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  refine ⟨g.image fun y => e.inv.val.app (op V) y, top_unique fun x _ => ?_⟩
  have key : ∀ y ∈ Submodule.span (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) (g : Set (N.val.obj (op V))),
      e.inv.val.app (op V) y ∈ Submodule.span (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V))
        ((g.image fun y => e.inv.val.app (op V) y : Finset (M.val.obj (op V))) :
          Set (M.val.obj (op V))) := by
    intro y hy
    induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem z hz =>
        exact Submodule.subset_span
          (Finset.mem_coe.mpr (Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨z, Finset.mem_coe.mp hz, rfl⟩))
    | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
    | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ ha hb
    | smul r a _ ha => rw [map_smul]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ha
  exact app_hom_app_inv_apply e.symm (op V) x ▸ key _ (hg ▸ trivial)

/-- **Finitely many sections span over a smaller open.** If a sheaf of modules is generated over
an open `W` by finitely many sections whose associated morphism out of the free sheaf is an
isomorphism, then its sections over any open `V ≤ W` are spanned by the restrictions of those
sections. -/
theorem exists_finset_span_of_generatingSections (E : X.Modules) (W V : X.Opens) (hV : V ≤ W)
    (σ : (E.over W).GeneratingSections) [Finite σ.I] [IsIso σ.π] :
    ∃ g : Finset (E.val.obj (op V)),
      Submodule.span (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V)) (g : Set (E.val.obj (op V))) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  have : Fintype σ.I := Fintype.ofFinite σ.I
  refine ⟨Finset.image
    (fun i : σ.I => ((σ.s i).eval (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hV))) : E.val.obj (op V)))
    Finset.univ, ?_⟩
  refine top_unique fun x _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_eq_sum_smul_freeHomEquiv σ.π
    (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hV)))
    ((asIso σ.π).inv.val.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hV))) x)
  replace ha := ha.trans (app_hom_app_inv_apply (asIso σ.π) (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hV))) x)
  have hmem : ∀ i : σ.I,
      ((E.over W).freeHomEquiv σ.π i).eval (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hV))) ∈
        Submodule.span (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V))
          ((Finset.image
            (fun i : σ.I => ((σ.s i).eval (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hV))) : E.val.obj (op V)))
            Finset.univ : Finset (E.val.obj (op V))) : Set (E.val.obj (op V))) := by
    intro i
    refine Submodule.subset_span (Finset.mem_coe.mpr (Finset.mem_image.mpr
      ⟨i, Finset.mem_univ i, ?_⟩))
    rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply]
  rw [← ha]
  exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (hmem i)

/-- **A finite locally free sheaf of modules is quasi-coherent**, the local free presentations
being presentations with no relations.

Mathlib has this as an instance for a locally free sheaf of modules over an arbitrary site, but
instance synthesis does not reach it from finite local freeness on the site of opens of a
scheme: the slice sheafification hypotheses of that instance are solved before its site is
determined, so this is stated again for a scheme, where those hypotheses hold. -/
instance isQuasicoherent_of_isFiniteLocallyFree (E : X.Modules)
    [h : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} E] : E.IsQuasicoherent := by
  obtain ⟨q, hq, -⟩ := h.exists_isFiniteLocallyFreeData
  let _ : q.IsLocallyFreeData := hq
  exact q.quasiCoherentData.isQuasicoherent

/-- **A finite locally free sheaf of modules is spanned by finitely many sections on an affine
open around every point.** The local free presentations of `E` live on a cover by arbitrary
opens, and the affine opens form a basis, so the presentation over a member of that cover
restricts to an affine open around any of its points. -/
theorem exists_affineOpen_finset_span (E : X.Modules)
    [h : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} E] (x : ↥X) :
    ∃ V : X.affineOpens, x ∈ V.1 ∧ ∃ g : Finset (E.val.obj (op V.1)),
      Submodule.span (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V.1)) (g : Set (E.val.obj (op V.1))) = ⊤ := by
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hqf⟩ := h.exists_isFiniteLocallyFreeData
  have hcover : ⨆ i, q.X i = ⊤ := (Opens.coversTop_iff X.carrier q.X).mp q.coversTop
  have hx : x ∈ ⨆ i, q.X i := hcover ▸ trivial
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Opens.mem_iSup.1 hx
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨V, hV, rfl⟩, hxV, hVW⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hi (q.X i).2
  have _ : IsIso (q.generators i).π := hq.isIso i
  have _ : Finite (q.generators i).I := (hqf.isFiniteType i).finite
  exact ⟨⟨V, hV⟩, hxV,
    exists_finset_span_of_generatingSections E (q.X i) V hVW (q.generators i)⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules

/-! ### Properness of a relative `Proj` from a cover of the base -/

namespace Stacks.RelativeProj

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} {A σ : S.affineOpens → Type u} [∀ U, CommRing (A U)]
  [∀ U, SetLike (σ U) (A U)] [∀ U, AddSubgroupClass (σ U) (A U)]
  {𝒜 : ∀ U, ℕ → σ U} [∀ U, GradedRing (𝒜 U)]

namespace Data

variable (d : Data 𝒜)

/-- A property of morphisms of schemes which is Zariski-local at the target holds for the
structure morphism of a relative `Proj` as soon as it holds for the charts over the members of a
family of affine opens covering the base. -/
theorem prop_toBase_of_cover (P : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) [IsZariskiLocalAtTarget P]
    {ι : Type*} (V : ι → S.affineOpens) (hV : ⨆ i, (V i : S.Opens) = ⊤)
    (h : ∀ i, P (chartToOpen 𝒜 (V i) (d.base (V i)))) : P d.toBase := by
  rw [IsZariskiLocalAtTarget.iff_of_iSup_eq_top (P := P) (fun i => ((V i : S.Opens))) hV]
  exact fun i => (d.prop_morphismRestrict_iff P (V i)).mpr (h i)

/-- **The structure morphism of a relative `Proj` is proper** when, over the members of a family
of affine opens covering the base, the degree-zero identification is an isomorphism and the
graded ring is a finite type algebra over its degree-zero part. -/
theorem isProper_toBase_of_cover {ι : Type*} (V : ι → S.affineOpens)
    (hV : ⨆ i, (V i : S.Opens) = ⊤) (hb : ∀ i, IsIso (d.base (V i)))
    (hft : ∀ i, Algebra.FiniteType (𝒜 (V i) 0) (A (V i))) : IsProper d.toBase :=
  d.prop_toBase_of_cover @IsProper V hV fun i =>
    have := hb i
    have := hft i
    (prop_chartToOpen_iff 𝒜 @IsProper (V i) (d.base (V i))).mpr inferInstance

end Data

/-! ### Finite type section rings from the section-level generation statement -/

namespace Situation

variable (s : Situation.{u})

/-- The degree-one part of the section ring over `U` lies in the subalgebra generated over the
degree-zero part by the images of finitely many spanning degree-one local sections. -/
theorem sectionRingGrading_one_le_adjoin (U : s.base.Opens) (g : Finset (s.sectionPieces U 1))
    (hg : Submodule.span (s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))
      (g : Set (s.sectionPieces U 1)) = ⊤) :
    (s.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) ⊆
      (Algebra.adjoin (s.sectionRingGrading U 0)
        ((fun x : s.sectionPieces U 1 => DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 1 x) ''
          (g : Set (s.sectionPieces U 1))) : Set (s.sectionRing U)) := by
  rintro z ⟨x, rfl⟩
  have hx : x ∈ Submodule.span (s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))
      (g : Set (s.sectionPieces U 1)) := hg ▸ trivial
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy => exact Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact Subalgebra.zero_mem _
  | add y w _ _ ihy ihw => rw [map_add]; exact Subalgebra.add_mem _ ihy ihw
  | smul r y _ ih =>
      have h0 : s.sectionRingBaseMap U r ∈
          Algebra.adjoin (s.sectionRingGrading U 0)
            ((fun x : s.sectionPieces U 1 => DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 1 x) ''
              (g : Set (s.sectionPieces U 1))) :=
        Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _
          (⟨s.sectionRingBaseMap U r, sectionRingBaseMap_mem_zero s U r⟩ :
            s.sectionRingGrading U 0)
      rw [← sectionRingBaseMap_mul_of s U 1 r y]
      exact Subalgebra.mul_mem _ h0 ih

/-- **The section ring over `U` is a finite type algebra over its degree-zero part**, as soon as
it is generated over that part by its degree-one piece and the degree-one local sections over `U`
are spanned by finitely many of them.

This is `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.finiteType_sectionRing` with the sheaf-level generation
hypothesis `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne` replaced by its consequence on
the section ring. For a symmetric algebra, whose homogeneous pieces are sheafifications, only the
consequence is available. -/
theorem finiteType_sectionRing_of_adjoin_eq_top (U : s.base.Opens)
    (hadjoin : Algebra.adjoin (s.sectionRingGrading U 0)
      (s.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) = ⊤)
    (g : Finset (s.sectionPieces U 1))
    (hg : Submodule.span (s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))
      (g : Set (s.sectionPieces U 1)) = ⊤) :
    Algebra.FiniteType (s.sectionRingGrading U 0) (s.sectionRing U) := by
  classical
  refine ⟨⟨g.image fun x => DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 1 x, ?_⟩⟩
  rw [Finset.coe_image]
  refine top_unique ?_
  rw [← hadjoin]
  exact Algebra.adjoin_le (sectionRingGrading_one_le_adjoin s U g hg)

/-- **The structure morphism of the relative projective spectrum of a situation is proper** when,
over the members of a family of affine opens covering the base, the degree-zero identification is
an isomorphism and the section ring is a finite type algebra over its degree-zero part. -/
theorem isProper_relativeProjToBase_of_cover {ι : Type*} (V : ι → s.base.affineOpens)
    (hV : ⨆ i, (V i : s.base.Opens) = ⊤)
    (hb : ∀ i, IsIso (sectionRingZeroMap s (V i).1))
    (hft : ∀ i, Algebra.FiniteType (s.sectionRingGrading (V i).1 0) (s.sectionRing (V i).1)) :
    IsProper (relativeProjToBase s) :=
  (chartData s).isProper_toBase_of_cover V hV hb hft

end Situation

/-! ### The projective bundle of a finite locally free module -/

variable (X : Scheme.{u}) (E : X.Modules)

/-- **The degree-zero identification of every chart of a projective bundle is an isomorphism.**
Degree zero of `Sym(E)` is the structure sheaf, with no hypothesis on `E` beyond
quasi-coherence. -/
theorem isIso_sectionRingZeroMap_symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent [E.IsQuasicoherent]
    (U : X.Opens) :
    IsIso (Situation.sectionRingZeroMap (symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E) U) :=
  (symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E).isIso_sectionRingZeroMap U
    ((symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E).bijective_smul_one_of_isoUnit
      (SheafOfModules.sheafifiedSymmetricPieceZeroIso (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) E)
      (fun W => SheafOfModules.sheafifiedSymmetricPieceZeroIso_one
        (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) E W) U)

/-- The degree-one local sections of `Sym(E)` over an open are spanned by finitely many of them
as soon as the local sections of `E` are, degree one of a symmetric algebra being the module
itself. -/
theorem exists_finset_span_sectionPieces_one [E.IsQuasicoherent] (U : X.Opens)
    (h : ∃ g : Finset (E.val.obj (op U)),
      Submodule.span (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U)) (g : Set (E.val.obj (op U))) = ⊤) :
    ∃ g : Finset ((symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E).sectionPieces U 1),
      Submodule.span
          ((symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E).base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))
        (g : Set ((symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E).sectionPieces U 1)) = ⊤ :=
  let ⟨g, hg⟩ := h
  AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.exists_finset_span_of_iso
    (SheafOfModules.sheafifiedSymmetricPieceOneIso (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) E) U g hg

/-- **The projection `π : 𝐏(ℰ) ⟶ X` of the projective bundle of a finite locally free sheaf of
modules is proper.**

This is the properness clause of Stacks 0800 for the graded algebra `Sym(ℰ)`: its degree-zero
part is the structure sheaf and it is generated in degree one by `ℰ`, which is spanned by
finitely many sections on a cover of `X` by affine opens. -/
@[stacks 0800 "proper, for the projective bundle of a finite locally free module"]
theorem isProper_projectiveBundleToBase
    [SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} E] :
    IsProper (projectiveBundleToBase X E) := by
  classical
  set T : Set X.affineOpens := {V | ∃ g : Finset (E.val.obj (op V.1)),
    Submodule.span (X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V.1)) (g : Set (E.val.obj (op V.1))) = ⊤} with hT
  have hcover : ⨆ V : T, (V.1.1 : X.Opens) = ⊤ := by
    refine eq_top_iff.2 fun x _ => ?_
    obtain ⟨V, hxV, hV⟩ :=
      AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.exists_affineOpen_finset_span E x
    exact Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨⟨V, hV⟩, hxV⟩
  refine (symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E).isProper_relativeProjToBase_of_cover
    (fun V : T => V.1) hcover
    (fun V => isIso_sectionRingZeroMap_symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E V.1.1)
    fun V => ?_
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_finset_span_sectionPieces_one X E V.1.1 V.2
  exact (symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E).finiteType_sectionRing_of_adjoin_eq_top V.1.1
    (adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top_symmetricSituationOfQuasicoherent X E V.1.1 V.1.2) g hg

end Stacks.RelativeProj

end
